  "slug": "archaea-duplication-d927",
  "summary": "Graph pangenomes now resolve structural variants in yeast isolates, while metagenomic variation graphs extend the approach to microbial communities.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is inference of structural and gene-content variation from pangenome-scale graphs rather than single reference genomes. A graph pangenome of 1060 Brettanomyces bruxellensis isolates detects 5972 SVs, with allopolyploids carrying more SVs and hybridization-associated SVs strongly affecting function. Comparative analysis of gut bacterial isolate genomes links industrialized-host strains to expanded proteomes and fluid pangenomes. PANIMaSTA, a progressive ANI and maximum-spanning-tree workflow, targets minimally fragmented metagenomic pangenome variation graphs and is applied to large metagenomic collections. PrinTE and VENAS2 address related evolutionary questions through forward simulation of TE dynamics and bidirectional mutation modeling, but are not pangenome methods; any connection to graph-based SV detection is complementary and not demonstrated here.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
